  "id": "hangover",
  "term": "hangover",
  "definition": "In this cognition context, a hangover refers to the lingering period after an acute hypoxic exposure when cognitive and some physiological functions have not yet fully returned to normal, even after normal oxygen levels are restored. These after-effects can last from minutes to hours, with most recovery usually occurring within about 2 to 4 hours.",
